{
  "id": "us-devaluation",
  "term": "US devaluation",
  "definition": "US devaluation is a procedure in Pavlovian conditioning that reduces the current value of the unconditioned stimulus, such as making water less valuable by giving it until satiation. It is used to test whether a conditioned response depends on the present value of that outcome.",
